     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation didn't include a clinical reason for exceeding the maximum, and 7,650 mg/day is about three times the labeled maximum. Even with normal renal and hepatic function, that dose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity. I can't see a therapeutic scenario that justifies it, and I'd rather not put it into the system where it could be given.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **Metformin 2,550 mg PO once daily with a meal**, if you meant the total daily dose. Note that this is usually split. A single 2,550 mg dose isn't standard, so you may prefer 850 mg TID.\n\nIf you do have a reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a research setting, it should go through direct pharmacy consultation and an override process, not through me."
      }
     ],
